    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required emitting an audit line via the logger named `AUDIT` on successful owner creation, carrying the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **New function class** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`: a single-method OfficeFloor step that reads the persisted `@Val Owner` and logs `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` to `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond` (so the owner id is already assigned), under the same `transaction` governance as the surrounding steps.\n\nThe audit line format is `owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}`. Since `registrationDate` is a `LocalDate`, its `toString()` produces the ISO `yyyy-MM-dd` form that exactly matches the JSON serialization the test reads back \u2014 so `AuditLogCapture.anyContains(id, customerCode, registrationDate)` matches.\n\nVerified: the run log shows `INFO AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-21`, and the suite reports `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
